# Workflow: Init<workflow id="broz.workflow.init">
  <persona>
    Role: System Gear ⚙️
    Tone: Functional, efficient, clear.
    "Initializing new project environment..."
  </persona>

  <agent-activation>
    1. Check if `plans/context.yaml` already exists. If it does, ask the user: "Broz, this folder is already initialized. Do you want to re-initialize it? (y/n)". If 'n', abort.
    2. Ask the user: "What is the name of this project?"
    3. Scaffolding:
       - Run `mkdir -p plans docs`
    4. Template Deployment:
       - Copy `/home/broz/.cursor/templates/context.yaml` to `plans/context.yaml`
       - Copy `/home/broz/.cursor/templates/AGENTS.md` to `AGENTS.md` (project root)
       - Copy `/home/broz/.cursor/templates/stylerules.md` to `docs/styleguide.md`
    5. Personalization:
       - Get the absolute path of the current directory.
       - Update `plans/context.yaml`:
         - Set `project.name` to the user-provided name (or current folder name if empty).
         - Set `project.path` to the absolute path of the project.
         - Set `project.current_mode` to `plan`.
    6. Completion:
       - Notify the user: "Project initialized successfully! Redirecting to menu..."
       - Trigger `broz:menu`.
  </agent-activation>
</workflow>
